The '''Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line''' is a high-speed rail line operated by [[Intercon]] that connects the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Sant Cristòfor]] with the [[Estació Central de Portnou]] in [[Portnou]], the two largest cities in [[Balboa]]. The line opened on 11 March 2009 as the second high-speed rail line in the country, following the [[Sant Cristòfor–Areza HSR line|Sant Cristòfor–Areza line]] by one year. It replaced the conventional [[Sant Cristòfor–Portnou Line|Sant Cristòfor–Portnou long-distance service]], reducing the end-to-end journey time from over 90 minutes to approximately 27 minutes.

The line is 99 km long and serves three stations under regular operation, with a fourth station served only during events at the [[Estadi de Balboa]]. Between Sant Cristòfor Central and [[Varakí TDV (CristoCarril)|Varakí TDV]], the line shares tracks with the [[Sant Cristòfor–Areza HSR line|Sant Cristòfor–Areza HSR line]], diverging south of Varakí onto a dedicated spur toward Portnou. The maximum operating speed is 250 km/h.

== Route ==

The Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line runs south from the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] through the [[Estret Province|Estret]] corridor to Varakí, then continues south to Portnou. The line serves three stations under regular operation:

